  "notes": {
    "vinMin": "The operating conditions on page 5 give 4.5 V for the family. The 3.3-V version's output regulation is specified over 4.75 V to 40 V (page 6); the lower figure is the device rating and the higher one is the condition its output limits are guaranteed under.",
    "voutFixed": "A fixed 3.3-V version: the feedback pin connects straight to the output, so the output voltage is the part number rather than a resistor divider.",
    "feedbackReference": "The 1.23-V feedback voltage on page 6 belongs to the adjustable version (section 7.8). The fixed 3.3-V version senses the output directly, and the datasheet states no reference for it.",
    "feedbackAccuracy": "Arithmetic on the stated output limits: 3.168 V and 3.432 V about 3.3 V is +/-4%. The datasheet states the limits, not the percentage, and the +/-4% on page 1 is quoted for the adjustable version.",
    "softStart": "Five pins, none of them a soft-start pin. The absolute maximum ratings table on page 5 lists SD/SS, Delay and Flag pins, which this device does not have; the pin functions table on page 4 is the one that describes the LM2596.",
    "lightLoadMode": "A fixed 150-kHz oscillator and no power-save or pulse-skipping mode anywhere in the datasheet.",
    "minOnTime": "No minimum on time is stated. The only duty-cycle limits are the 100% maximum and 0% minimum on page 7.",
    "efficiencyPeak": "The only efficiency figure for the 3.3-V version is 73% at VIN = 12 V and ILOAD = 3 A, which is a full-load point rather than a peak. The typical characteristics show curves; reading a peak off one would be a guess.",
    "rdsOnHigh": "This is a bipolar switch specified by saturation voltage: 1.16 V typical at 3 A. There is no on-resistance in the datasheet.",
    "rdsOnLow": "Non-synchronous: the low side is an external catch diode, so the device has no low-side switch.",
    "thermalPad": "The TO-263 tab is the thermal path, and the thermal information on page 5 specifies the junction-to-ambient resistance by how much copper the tab is soldered to.",
    "package": "The orderable addendum gives the package as DDPAK/TO-263 (KTT) with five pins, in a 45-piece tube. The tape-and-reel orderable is LM2596SX-3.3/NOPB.",
    "aecQ100": "No automotive-qualified orderable and no AEC-Q100 claim anywhere in the datasheet."
  },
